  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.caption.morphology_record": "Morphology Record",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.anglerfish.paragraph_1": "Field observation records a predatory lure used to draw closer targets into range.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.anglerfish.paragraph_2": "The species holds position for long intervals and advances only when a target is close enough.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.catfish.paragraph_1": "Bottom survey confirms a seabed-oriented species that navigates by touch and current cues.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.catfish.paragraph_2": "Behavior is opportunistic and efficient, with a clear preference for sheltered routes and debris fields.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.creeporpedo.paragraph_1": "The specimen remains visually quiet while storing charge, which makes its threat level easy to underestimate.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.creeporpedo.paragraph_2": "When stimulated, it releases stored force abruptly and leaves little time for a second response.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.donutfish.paragraph_1": "Distinctive ring-shaped specimen with calm movement and no aggressive response during initial contact.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.donutfish.paragraph_2": "Feeding notes classify it as a low-risk grazer that remains predictable under routine observation.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.electrofish.paragraph_1": "Ambient water registers charge before direct visual contact, indicating a strongly reactive species.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.electrofish.paragraph_2": "The specimen feeds on motion and resistance, and it keeps nearby currents disturbed even at rest.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.giant_abyss_worm.paragraph_1": "Titan-class trench specimen. Its emergence disrupts local current structure across a wide area.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.giant_abyss_worm.paragraph_2": "The body is segmented and heavily mobile, so field work should prioritize distance and exit routes.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.giant_octopus_tentacle.paragraph_1": "A single limb sample is enough to confirm titan-scale reach before the full body is visible.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.giant_octopus_tentacle.paragraph_2": "Observed behaviors are probing, gripping, and retrieval, all consistent with a much larger host organism.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.gloomgazer.paragraph_1": "Low-light predator that reduces visible contrast in the surrounding water as it approaches.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.gloomgazer.paragraph_2": "It waits motionless in dim areas and relies on patient ambush rather than pursuit.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.helicoprion.paragraph_1": "Ancient predatory specimen with a spiral jaw structure and no sign of behavioral moderation.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.helicoprion.paragraph_2": "The jaw assembly is the primary hazard and appears specialized for forceful contact at close range.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.icerail.paragraph_1": "Cold-water glider with motion tuned to low temperatures and minimal surface disturbance.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.icerail.paragraph_2": "Performance drops outside chilled currents, so temperature is a key environmental variable.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.lighting_worm.paragraph_1": "Electrically active worm-like specimen that announces itself through a clear voltage signature.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.lighting_worm.paragraph_2": "The species converts ambient charge into sustained motion and remains active around conductive water.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.manta_ray.paragraph_1": "Large gliding specimen that maintains broad, level passes through open water.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.manta_ray.paragraph_2": "The body plan favors pressure tolerance and efficient travel over acceleration or aggression.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.octopus.paragraph_1": "Armed survey specimen. It tests the environment before committing to a route.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.octopus.paragraph_2": "Behavior is cautious and methodical, with strong preference for cover, texture, and timing.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.oxygen_breeder.paragraph_1": "Utility species that improves local water conditions rather than competing with nearby life.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.oxygen_breeder.paragraph_2": "Metabolic output appears to create usable oxygen, making the species valuable in confined systems.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.radioanemone.paragraph_1": "Signal-emitting reef organism that alters nearby water behavior before direct contact.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.radioanemone.paragraph_2": "It appears to consume and emit the same energy class, keeping the immediate area in a constant pulse state.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.red_jellyfish.paragraph_1": "Visually prominent stinging specimen. Light output is not a reliable indicator of safety.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.red_jellyfish.paragraph_2": "Disturbance triggers an immediate defensive strike, so close handling should be minimized.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.ringfish.paragraph_1": "Loop-shaped herbivore that turns in regular arcs and keeps to steady water.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.ringfish.paragraph_2": "Observed behavior is calm and predictable, with little deviation from a slow circuit pattern.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.sardine.paragraph_1": "Schooling sample. Individuals remain tightly synchronized and change direction as a unit.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.sardine.paragraph_2": "Low-mass herbivore with strong group cohesion; record density and spacing rather than single specimens.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.springfish.paragraph_1": "Compact, high-mobility specimen that stores energy in a coiled posture.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.springfish.paragraph_2": "The species displays abrupt jumps and resists prolonged restraint, so handling windows are short.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.swirl_maker.paragraph_1": "Current-distorting specimen. Water flow becomes unstable before direct contact is made.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.swirl_maker.paragraph_2": "The organism sustains a local vortex pattern with minimal movement, which complicates navigation.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.tripod.paragraph_1": "Three-point titan specimen. Its balance is unusual and remains stable under load.",
  "gui.aquanaut.notebook.waterlife.tripod.paragraph_2": "Motion is deliberate and mechanically regular, suggesting a structure optimized for sustained movement."
}
